Note: 

Please DO NOT read these logs as a purely linear or chronological conversation sequence. 
The actual cognitive process behind them was highly non-linear. For example,

* Prompt A may appear to be an "early-stage question", because A is in an "earlier" chat.
* But in reality, I might ask prompt A when I finished another prompt B in a "later" chat.

In addition, the dataset is inherently “incomplete”, some prompts got lost permanently because,

* The author failed to log in ChatGPT/Gemini at the time of generation...
* Some accidental deletion of chat history...
* Other reasons...

As a result, the chat history does not represent a complete trace of the author's cognitive process.
I INTENTIONALLY preserve the chat history to record my transient exploratory leaps made during the research.

Directory Structure:

* `history/`: Conversations in PDF format.
* `corpus/`: Some supporting textual materials, references, and background documentation.
* `images/`: Some prompt photos, diagrams, AI generated images, etc.
